"guided.foundation.intro.title" = "Find Gentle Control";
"guided.foundation.intro.body" = "Begin with natural breathing. Imagine gently lifting inward and upward as if holding back gas. Keep the movement small, and stop if it hurts.";
"guided.foundation.reflect.body" = "Was the contraction gentle? Did you fully let go afterward? There is no score to give yourself.";
"guided.coordinate.intro.title" = "Coordinate with Breath";
"guided.coordinate.intro.body" = "Keep your shoulders, abdomen, and glutes relaxed. Gently contract only while exhaling, then fully release while inhaling.";
"guided.coordinate.breathe.body" = "Observe a few breaths: let your abdomen expand on the inhale and settle slowly on the exhale.";
"guided.coordinate.reflect.body" = "Notice whether breathing stayed easy during movement. Next time, choose less effort rather than holding your breath.";

"guided.breathing.intro.title" = "Slow the Pace";
"guided.breathing.intro.body" = "Choose a supported position. There is no contraction or performance target here—only breathing and release.";
"guided.breathing.slow.body" = "Let the inhale move naturally into your abdomen and side ribs. Make the exhale slightly longer without forcing a deep breath.";
"guided.breathing.scan.body" = "Notice your jaw, shoulders, abdomen, and pelvic floor in turn. When you find tension, allow it to soften.";
"guided.breathing.release.body" = "With each exhale, use a little less effort and let the support beneath you carry your weight.";
"guided.breathing.reflect.body" = "How does tension compare with when you began? Simply notice; immediate improvement is not required.";
"guided.release.intro.title" = "Practice Letting Go";
"guided.release.intro.body" = "Today's goal is not more force. It is noticing unnecessary tension and allowing it to leave.";
"guided.release.breathe.body" = "Breathe naturally and notice whether your abdomen or glutes remain braced at the end of each exhale.";
"guided.release.scan.body" = "Scan from your face down to your pelvis. Wherever you find tension, reduce active effort slightly.";
"guided.release.practice.body" = "Imagine the pelvic floor as a hammock that widens naturally on the inhale and stays soft on the exhale.";
"guided.release.reflect.body" = "Which area held tension most easily? Begin your next practice by softening there.";

"guided.scan.intro.title" = "Observe Without Judging";
"guided.scan.intro.body" = "This is not a performance test. Notice contact, temperature, breathing, and tension as they are right now.";
"guided.scan.breathe.body" = "Settle with a few comfortable breaths without trying to control the result.";
"guided.scan.practice.body" = "Move attention slowly from your feet and legs through your pelvis, abdomen, chest, and shoulders. Notice without changing anything.";
"guided.scan.reflect.body" = "Name one neutral sensation you noticed, such as warmth, weight, contact, or a shift in breathing.";
"guided.rhythm.intro.title" = "Find an Easy Rhythm";
"guided.rhythm.intro.body" = "The goal is steadiness and comfort, not lasting longer. You can slow down at any time.";
"guided.rhythm.breathe.body" = "Find an effortless breathing rhythm and let the exhale run slightly longer than the inhale.";
"guided.rhythm.scan.body" = "Notice whether anticipation makes you brace early. If it does, return attention to support and breathing.";
"guided.rhythm.release.body" = "Release judgment about the outcome and let your body return to a natural, sustainable rhythm.";
"guided.rhythm.reflect.body" = "Which rhythm felt most settled? Remember the sensation rather than a number you must reach.";

"guided.partner.intro.title" = "Pause Together";
"guided.partner.intro.body" = "Place the device where both people can see it. Answers are not recorded, and no intimate details are required.";
"guided.partner.reset.intro.title" = "Settle Before Sharing";
"guided.partner.reset.intro.body" = "Take turns reading. While one person speaks, the other listens. Either person may pause at any time.";
"guided.partner.consent.title" = "Confirm Willingness First";
"guided.partner.consent.body" = "Each person should clearly say whether they want to continue. Silence is not consent, and changing your mind needs no explanation.";
"guided.partner.breathe.title" = "Breathe Together";
"guided.partner.breathe.body" = "You do not need to synchronize perfectly. Simply slow down together while keeping your own breath comfortable.";
"guided.partner.reset.breathe.body" = "Take a few natural breaths each. Notice the other person's presence without needing to match them.";
"guided.partner.share.title" = "One-Sentence Check-In";
"guided.partner.share.body" = "Take turns answering in one sentence: would continuing, slowing down, or pausing feel best? Listen without persuading.";
"guided.partner.speaker.title" = "Share One Need";
"guided.partner.speaker.body" = "One person uses “Right now I need…” to name a boundary, pace, or kind of support without guessing for the other person.";
"guided.partner.listener.title" = "Reflect What You Heard";
"guided.partner.listener.body" = "The listener repeats what they understood and asks, “Did I get that right?” Avoid explaining or arguing for now.";
"guided.partner.finish.title" = "Close Gently";
"guided.partner.finish.body" = "Each person checks their comfort level. You may continue talking or end here.";
"guided.partner.reset.finish.body" = "Each say whether you need to continue, slow down, or pause. Respect every answer; finishing this exercise is not a commitment.";

"guided.progressive.foundation.steady.focus" = "Keep breathing naturally and use about thirty percent effort. Let every release last longer than the contraction.";
"guided.progressive.foundation.steady.reflect" = "Which round made breathing and full release easiest? Begin with that level of effort next time.";
"guided.progressive.foundation.endurance.focus" = "Endurance comes from sustainable gentle control, not holding your breath or pushing. Reduce effort when other muscles take over.";
"guided.progressive.foundation.endurance.reflect" = "Could you release as easily at the end as at the start? If not, shorten the hold next time.";
"guided.progressive.foundation.transfer.focus" = "Notice whether your abdomen, glutes, or jaw compensate as position changes. Keep only a small pelvic-floor movement.";
"guided.progressive.foundation.transfer.reflect" = "Which position made coordination easiest? Consolidate there before adding more variation.";
"guided.progressive.foundation.maintenance.focus" = "Move from light to slightly stronger and back to light, confirming a complete release after every round.";
"guided.progressive.foundation.maintenance.reflect" = "Does your body need maintenance, a lighter dose, or recovery today? Put comfort before completion.";
"guided.progressive.relaxation.downshift.focus" = "Use less effort in your jaw and shoulders, then let the exhale soften your abdomen and pelvic floor.";
"guided.progressive.relaxation.downshift.reflect" = "What softened first? You can use that area as an entry point next time.";
"guided.progressive.relaxation.wholebody.focus" = "Move through your face, chest, abdomen, glutes, and pelvic floor. At each stop, simply reduce effort.";
"guided.progressive.relaxation.wholebody.reflect" = "Which areas tense together? Noticing the connection is enough; you do not need to force a change.";
"guided.progressive.relaxation.recovery.focus" = "Keep breathing at an ordinary depth and notice neutral signals such as support, weight, and temperature.";
"guided.progressive.relaxation.recovery.reflect" = "Is stopping a little easier than when you began? Even a small change is useful feedback.";
"guided.progressive.relaxation.restorative.focus" = "Stay supported and free of targets. When an urge to work appears, return to a natural exhale.";
"guided.progressive.relaxation.restorative.reflect" = "Do you need activity or more recovery space now? Respect the answer your body gives.";
"guided.progressive.confidence.pressure.focus" = "When a need to perform appears, do not argue with it. Return attention to breathing and physical contact.";
"guided.progressive.confidence.pressure.reflect" = "When did pressure ease slightly? Remember the body cues present in that moment.";
"guided.progressive.confidence.sensation.focus" = "Choose one neutral signal—temperature, weight, touch, or breath—and rest attention there gently.";
"guided.progressive.confidence.sensation.reflect" = "Can you describe one sensation without rating it? That matters more than scoring performance.";
"guided.progressive.confidence.flexible.focus" = "Practice choosing among continuing, slowing, and pausing. Changing pace is regulation, not failure.";
"guided.progressive.confidence.flexible.reflect" = "Which adjustment made your body more comfortable? Carry that choice into your next practice.";
"guided.progressive.confidence.selftrust.focus" = "Hear the body signal before choosing an action. You do not need fixed numbers to prove progress.";
"guided.progressive.confidence.selftrust.reflect" = "Which body signal did you respect today? That is part of building trust.";
"guided.progressive.partner.boundaries.focus" = "Take turns naming one willing yes, one not-now boundary, and the support you need.";
"guided.progressive.partner.boundaries.reflect" = "Which wording made boundaries clearer without blame? Keep that phrasing available.";
"guided.progressive.partner.pace.focus" = "Take turns answering continue, slow down, or pause. Acknowledge the answer before explaining anything.";
"guided.progressive.partner.pace.reflect" = "Did both people truly have room to change the pace? Every no deserves respect.";
"guided.progressive.partner.repair.focus" = "One person describes what happened and how it felt; the other reflects their understanding. Confirm, then switch roles.";
"guided.progressive.partner.repair.reflect" = "Which reflection helped each person feel understood? Repair does not require immediate agreement.";
"guided.progressive.partner.choice.focus" = "Each offer options to continue, adjust, or stop, then look for the overlap both people freely want.";
"guided.progressive.partner.choice.reflect" = "Did the final choice come from clear agreement by both people? When there is no overlap, pausing is a complete decision.";

